{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder","id":1178503,"title":"1000 Years of Night: What's an Elder?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-23T12:06:19-08:00","id":1178503,"title":"1000 Years of Night: What's an Elder?","content":"Am I missing something, or is this term never <b>actually</b> defined, despite being a prerequisite for a massive number of things in the book? I have a Daeva vampire (En) that through diablerie is now sitting at BP 9, despite not being an 'elder' as far as age goes.<br /> <br /> Should this character suffer the Elder clan bane? Because the Wanton Curse has basically no impact on Elders. Should they be able to acquire merits and other powers that have a pre-requisite of Elder? Is 'Elder' really about age, or is it about Potency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T12:12:57-08:00","id":1178506,"title":"","content":"&quot;elder: A vampire who has survived for over 150 years; also<br /> a term of respect.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2ed core p.74","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T12:15:44-08:00","id":1178507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder?p=1178506#post1178506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;elder: A vampire who has survived for over 150 years; also a term of respect.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2ed core p.74</div> </div> </div> </div>Straightforward enough that this probably could have gone into the simple questions thread. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T13:02:56-08:00","id":1178516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder#post1178503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should this character suffer the Elder clan bane? Because the Wanton Curse has basically no impact on Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>The larger question's already been answered, but it's worth remembering that feeding restrictions aren't a hard denial of Vitae in 2e \u2014 elders who eschew Kindred Vitae may need to lean into the extremes of their Anchors more to make a net gain, but it's fully possible for a vampire of a certain age to sustain themselves without courting monsters for their fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T13:03:40-08:00","id":1178518,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure and I'm too lazy to check right now, but I think the exact age changes with geography and culture. European colonialism and all that... So, in northern America, an elder is 150 years+ while in, for example, Italy, it would be closer to 250 simply because of older cities.<br /> <br /> I seriously have a feeling like I read that somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23744-malkav-s-weird-cousin","name":"Malkav's Weird Cousin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T13:27:32-08:00","id":1178529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkav's Weird Cousin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder?p=1178518#post1178518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure and I'm too lazy to check right now, but I think the exact age changes with geography and culture. European colonialism and all that... So, in northern America, an elder is 150 years+ while in, for example, Italy, it would be closer to 250 simply because of older cities.<br /> <br /> I seriously have a feeling like I read that somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masquerade?<br /> <br /> Then again, even if that\u2019s a Masquerade thing, it works in Requiem as well. I can easily imagine a 200-year old vampire referring to her 400-year old sire as \u201celder\u201d and not referring to herself as \u201celder\u201d in front of him and his peers, simply to respect the ancient monsters. Her minions and childre, on the other hand, will refer to all of them as elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:09:40-08:00","id":1178546,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the &quot;less time requisites to qualify as X&quot; in the New World versus Europe is a Masquerade thing. Same as elder meaning something different, I think a lot of people were a bit dissapointed about the elders in TYON because they were expecting Ancients (vampires that &quot;lived&quot; for over a thousand years)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:32:44-08:00","id":1178553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder?p=1178546#post1178546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the &quot;less time requisites to qualify as X&quot; in the New World versus Europe is a Masquerade thing. Same as elder meaning something different, I think a lot of people were a bit dissapointed about the elders in TYON because they were expecting Ancients (vampires that &quot;lived&quot; for over a thousand years)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, when you consider the <i>name</i> of the book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:32:45-08:00","id":1178554,"title":"","content":"It's in the name of the book! Kidding, I don't particularly like the concept of X Ancients running around in the same place. In my games, they're usually crushed by the weight of their years and kill themselves, sometimes by way of funeral pyre. It's a big social faux pas if you're invited to an Ancient's funeral and don't show up.<br /> <br /> As for elders, yeah, could be I read it in one of the six million Masquerade books that came out over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23744-malkav-s-weird-cousin","name":"Malkav's Weird Cousin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T16:41:43-08:00","id":1178591,"title":"","content":"I suppose Hundreds Years of Night doesn't roll that well on the tongue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:48:45-08:00","id":1178743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder?p=1178591#post1178591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose Hundreds Years of Night doesn't roll that well on the tongue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Hundred and Fifty Years of Night even less so.<br /> <br /> At 150+ years, a Vamp should have a minimum (baring Torpor reduction) of Blood Potency 4, which curiously isn't even the point at which they require Vitae to feed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:36:57-08:00","id":1178759,"title":"","content":"Yep, that would be the minimum but remember that an active Requiem can accelerate the rate at wich Blood Potency increases (as represented by Experiences). To be fair, Elders are suppossed to be any from that 150 mark up to the 1000 one, when they would start to be considered Ancients, so there is going to be a lot of variation, specially considering Torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T06:51:00-08:00","id":1178768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder?p=1178759#post1178759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, that would be the minimum but remember that an active Requiem can accelerate the rate at wich Blood Potency increases (as represented by Experiences). To be fair, Elders are suppossed to be any from that 150 mark up to the 1000 one, when they would start to be considered Ancients, so there is going to be a lot of variation, specially considering Torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know - that's why I said minimum. Regarding the 1000 year mark, mechanically a Vampire that manages to stave off BP-reducing Torpor (and doesn't spend any XPs on it) will hit Blood Potency 10 by year 450. Long before the &quot;Ancient&quot; label.<br /> <br /> Just thought I'd point out the mechanics vs the terminology/titles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:06:03-08:00","id":1178770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1178503-1000-years-of-night-what-s-an-elder?p=1178743#post1178743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hundred and Fifty Years of Night even less so.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Hundred Years of Night wouldn't sound bad, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T07:21:58-08:00","id":1178774,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it sounds better and better the more I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}